Description: hw/nvram: Add the Atmel AT25080A SPI EEPROM
 The Chumby Classic's sensor card has a 1 KiB SPI EEPROM, the "DC ID"
 EEPROM, which the stock driver (drivers/char/chumby_accel.c, "DC ID
 EEPROM driver version 1.0-Atmel-25080A") reads at boot for
 /proc/DCversion and offers to user space through /dev/dcid ioctls
 (read, write, read status, lock, unlock). It uses the SPI serial EEPROM
 instruction set: RDSR (0x05) to poll the busy bit, READ (0x03) and
 WRITE (0x02) with a 16-bit address, WREN (0x06) and WRDI (0x04) around
 writes, and WRSR (0x01).
 .
 Model an AT25080A: 1024 x 8, opcodes with bit 3 a don't-care, the low
 10 address bits used, READ running on through the array and WRITE
 wrapping within a 32-byte page. Writes need the write latch and finish
 at once, so the busy bit never shows; a completed WRITE or WRSR clears
 the latch. The block-protect bits guard the top quarter, half or all
 of the array; WPEN is kept but the WP pin is not modelled. An address
 loaded from a migration stream is checked to be in range.
 .
 The contents are not file-backed: at25080a_program() sets them when
 the board is built, as if programmed at the factory, and guest writes
 last until QEMU exits.
